SOURCE="Philippine Statistics Authority, 2024 Census of Population";
NOTEX="<strong>Definition:</strong>#Total population defines as the sum of the household population and the institutional population, covering all persons living within a specific territory at a given reference time, including Filipinos in embassies or missions"
" abroad.#Household Population: All persons who are members of a private household, meaning a person or group of persons sleeping in the same housing unit with common arrangements for food preparation and consumption. #Institutional Population: Persons li"
"ving in institutional living quarters (ILQs) such as penal/corrective institutions, dormitories, hotels, military camps, or welfare facilities.#Household is defined as a social unit consisting of a person or a group of persons who sleep in the same housi"
"ng unit and have a common arrangement in the preparation and consumption of food.#Average Household Size is defined as the average number of persons residing in a household, obtained by dividing the household population by the number of households.##<str"
"ong>Method of Computation:</strong> Average Household Size is calculated by dividing the total household population by the total number of households.##<strong>Source of Basic Data:</strong> 2024 Census of Population##<strong>Level of Disaggregation:</st"
"rong> Region, Province and Highly Urbanized City##<strong>Note/s:</strong>##*    Population counts for the provinces exclude the counts of Highly Urbanized Cities.#** Not a Province/HUC#a/  Population counts for the regions do not add up to the national "
"total. Includes 1,708 Filipinos in Philippine embassies, consulates, and mission abroad.#1/ Excludes 10 barangays transferred to the City of Taguig, in accordance with the Supreme Court decision in General Register (GR) 235316 dated 01 December 2021.#2/ "
"Includes 10 barangays transferred from the City of Makati, in accordance with the Supreme Court decision in GR 235316 dated 01 December 2021.#3/  Re-established into a region under Republic Act (RA) No. 12000 dated 11 June 2024.#4/ Transferred province u"
"nder RA No. 12000; taken from Region VI - Western Visayas.#5/ Transferred province under RA No. 12000; taken from Region VII - Central Visayas.#6/ Reassigned from BARMM to Region IX under Executive Order No. 91, dated July 30, 2025, per a Supreme Court r"
"uling on September 9, 2024.#7/ Created into a province through the division of the Province of Maguindanao under RA No. 11550; ratified on 17 September 2022.#8/ Renamed from Interim Province; comprised of eight newly created municipalities under the Bang"
"samoro Autonomy Act Nos. 41 to 48 dated 15 September 2022; ratified on 13 April 2024.";
